hey las vegas now snacking gets a bad  rap but it shouldn't snacking can be a  smart way to help fill in nutrient gaps  keep energy levels up and support weight  management today i have healthy snack  ideas for sweet and savory lovers  including homemade snack boxes and  grab-and-go options first what makes up  a healthy snack a healthy snack should  be low in added sugar fat and sodium and  instead focused on protein and fiber  which will keep you satisfied and  energized between meals there are many  grab-and-go dietitian approved options  for when you need something quick and  easy such as freeze-dried fruit with a  handful of nuts hummus with sliced  veggies or salsa with chips like the new  atkins protein chips which have 13 grams  of protein per bag and 4 grams of fiber  they come in nacho cheese and ranch with  the salty savory crunchy wanton chips  but without the carbs find them at  walmart walmart.com next up we have  satisfying sweet and savory snack boxes  four ways to make a mediterranean snack  box add whole grain pita sliced cucumber  and cherry tomatoes olives almonds and  hummus i use the new creamy fresh  cravings hummus because it's made with a  short list of high quality whole food  ingredients like chilean extra virgin  olive oil chickpeas and savory tahini  you can find the classic roasted red  pepper and roasted garlic flavors at  walmart for this salsa snack box add  sliced bell peppers a hard boiled egg  protein chips and salsa the fresh  cravings salsa is refrigerated instead  of jarred you can find the chunky and  restaurant style salsa in a range of  heat levels chilled in the produce  section at walmart if you're craving  sweet over savory simply swap out  veggies in your snack box for fruit  which just like veggies is a source of  fiber vitamins minerals and antioxidants  to make this chocolate yogurt box whisk  together a third cup of plain greek  yogurt with one teaspoon of honey and  one teaspoon of cocoa powder add whole  grain low 